From 9afbf230fcce5ccab4d75d93a89560d2cb9c587d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Fennell <2501251+timfennell@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:23:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Training animation capture: record the model while it trains

A "Training animation capture" panel on the trainer screen renders the
model on the training thread between steps, from cameras of its own, so the
live preview is untouched: fixed training views, an arc through several
views (position, up and look-at target interpolated, so it stays on the
subject), and/or an orbit about the scene, several tracks at once.

Frames go to <run>/captures/<track>/ as PNG sequences (HD, 2K or 4K, RGBA
or over black) and/or H.264/H.265 video piped to ffmpeg; frames.csv maps
frames to steps. A frame every N steps, five times as often at the start.
It reuses the trainer's forward, so it costs about 10 MB of GPU memory and
0.37 s per 4K frame on an M2 Pro; encoding runs on writer threads.

See docs/notes/training-capture.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
